\"Jaffa\",\"Jean-Antoine Verdier\",\"Jean-Baptiste Kléber\",\"Jean Lannes\",\"Joachim Murat\",\"Juan Cole\",\"Kingdom of France\",\"Kingdom of Great Britain\",\"Kör Yusuf Ziyaüddin Pasha\",\"List of Ottoman battles in World War I\",\"List of Ottoman battles in the 20th century\",\"List of battles involving the Ottoman Empire\",\"Louis-François Lejeune\",\"Louis-Nicolas Davout\",\"Louis Desaix\",\"Muhammad Ali of Egypt\",\"Mustafa Pasha (Egypt)\",\"Nafisa al-Bayda\",\"Napoleon\",\"Napoleon I of France\",\"Natron\",\"Naval actions at the siege of Ochakov (1788)\",\"Naval gunfire support\",\"Night attack at Târgoviște\",\"OCLC (identifier)\",\"Ottoman Egypt\",\"Ottoman Empire\",\"Ottoman Old Regime\",\"Ottoman conquest of Adrianople\",\"Ottoman raid on the Balearic Islands (1501)\",\"Ottoman–Safavid War (1532–1555)\",\"Ottoman–Venetian War (1570–1573)\",\"PMID (identifier)\",\"Paris\",\"Patrona Bey\",\"Prisoner of war\",\"Pruth River Campaign\",\"Revolt of Cairo\",\"Rise of the Ottoman Empire\",\"Rosetta\",\"Rowman & Littlefield\",\"Royal Marines\",\"Royal Navy\",\"Russo-Turkish War (1787–1792)\",\"Second Battle of Zrínyiújvár\",\"Second Siege of El Arish\",\"Selim III\",\"Sidney Smith (Royal Navy officer)\",\"Siege of Acre (1799)\",\"Siege of Akka (1832)\",\"Siege of Alexandria (1801)\",\"Siege of Belgrade (1456)\",\"Siege of Belgrade (1717)\",\"Siege of Bihać (1592)\",\"Siege of Buda (1684)\",\"Siege of Cairo\",\"Siege of Candia\",\"Siege of El Arish\",\"Siege of El Rahmaniya\",\"Siege of Esztergom (1543)\",\"Siege of Fort Julien\",\"Siege of Ganja (1734)\",\"Siege of Giurgiu (1790)\",\"Siege of Golubac\",\"Siege of Gvozdansko\",\"Siege of Izmail\",\"Siege of Jaffa\",\"Siege of Jeddah\",\"Siege of Kars\",\"Siege of Kars (1828)\",\"Siege of Krupa\",\"Siege of Kulaca Hisar\",\"Siege of Nagykanizsa\",\"Siege of Negroponte (1688)\",\"Siege of Nicaea (1328–1331)\",\"Siege of Novi Zrin (1664)\",\"Siege of Novo Brdo (1440–1441)\",\"Siege of Ochakov (1737)\",\"Siege of Ochakov (1788)\",\"Siege of Ohrid (1395)\",\"Siege of Oran (1707–1708)\",\"Siege of Perekop (1736)\",\"Siege of Pest\",\"Siege of Plevna\",\"Siege of Shkodra\",\"Siege of Szigetvár\",\"Siege of Temesvár (1552)\",\"Siege of Thessalonica (1422–1430)\",\"Siege of Varna (1828)\",\"Suleiman al-Halabi\",\"Tahmasp's campaign of 1731\",\"Transformation of the Ottoman Empire\",\"Tug (banner)\",\"Upper Egypt\",\"Uprising in Banat\",\"Vendée\",\"William Pitt the Younger\",\"Wounded in action\",\"École militaire\",\"Template talk:Campaignbox Egypt-Syria\",\"Template talk:Ottoman battles\"],\"blacklist\":[],\"lastLinkClicked\":\"Battle of Abukir (1799)\"},\"feedback\":1.1925223877458753},{\"t\":2,\"state\":{\"currentTitle\":\"Battle of Abukir (1799)\",\"summary\":\"The Battle of Abukir (also known as the Battle of Aboukir or Battle of Abu Qir) was fought on 25 July 1799 between the French Army of the Orient under Napoleon and an Ottoman army under Mustafa Pasha during the French invasion of Egypt and Syria. It is considered the first pitched battle with this name, as there already had been a naval battle on 1 August 1798, the Battle of the Nile. (A second pitched battle followed on 8 March 1801.)\\nNo sooner had the French forces returned from a campaign to Syria, than the Ottoman forces were transported to Egypt by an Anglo-Ottoman fleet under Sidney Smith to put an end to French rule in Egypt. Pasha was an experienced commander who had fought against the Russians. He knew that cavalry charges against the French squares were futile. So, he sought to avoid them by fortifying his beachhead with two defensive lines. From this beachhead Pasha could carry out the invasion of Egypt. However, Napoleon immediately saw the flaw in the tactic as it meant that the Ottomans had nowhere to run if routed.\\nThe French attacked the Ottoman positions and quickly broke through the first defensive line before it was fully completed. The second line, however, proved tougher to defeat and the French withdrew for a while. At this point, cavalry general Murat saw his opportunity and attacked with his cavalry, quickly routing the exposed Ottomans. Murat's charge was so rapid that he burst inside Pasha's tent and captured him, severing two of his fingers with his sabre. In return, Pasha shot Murat in the jaw. Immediately, Murat was operated on and resumed his duties the next day.\\nThe Ottoman army fled in panic. Some Ottomans drowned trying to swim to the British ships two miles away from shore, while others fled to Abukir castle, but they surrendered shortly thereafter. The Ottoman army was annihilated, while French losses were under 1,000. News of the victory reached France before Napoleon arrived in October and this made him even more popular, an important asset considering the troubles brewing in the French Directory. This battle temporarily secured France's control over Egypt.\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle%20of%20Abukir%20(1799)\",\"goal\":\"French Revolution\",\"history\":[\"Battle of Vienna\",\"Battle of Abukir (1799)\"],\"depth\":2,\"links\":[\"Abu Qir\",\"Acre, Israel\",\"Adana campaign\",\"Al-Hasa Expedition 1871\",\"Alexandria\",\"Algiers expedition (1541)\",\"Antoine-Jean Gros\",\"Antoine de Phélippeaux\",\"Arc de Triomphe\",\"Armée d'Orient (1798) order of battle\",\"Auguste de Marmont\",\"Azov campaigns (1695–96)\",\"Barnsley\",\"Battle at Jurjeve Stijene\",\"Battle of Aboukir (Lejeune)\",\"Battle of Abukir (1801)\",\"Battle of Abukir (disambiguation)\",\"Battle of Akhaltsikhe\",\"Battle of Akhaltsikhe (1853)\",\"Battle of Al-Safra\",\"Battle of Al Khankah\",\"Battle of Al Wajbah\",\"Battle of Aladzha\",\"Battle of Alamana\",\"Battle of Alborán\",\"Battle of Albulena\",\"Battle of Alcácer Quibir\",\"Battle of Alexandria (1801)\",\"Battle of Andros (1696)\",\"Battle of Andros (1790)\",\"Battle of Ankara\",\"Battle of Arachova\",\"Battle of Arpachai\",\"Battle of Aspindza\",\"Battle of Athos\",\"Battle of Banja Luka\",\"Battle of Bapheus\",\"Battle of Batin\",\"Battle of Batočina\",\"Battle of Başgedikler\",\"Battle of Beirut (1520)\",\"Battle of Bileća\",\"Battle of Breadfield\",\"Battle of Brest (1592)\",\"Battle of Brest (1596)\",\"Battle of Cape Celidonia\",\"Battle of Cape Corvo\",\"Battle of Cape Kaliakra\",\"Battle of Cecora (1620)\",\"Battle of Chaldiran\",\"Battle of Chelif\",\"Battle of Călugăreni\",\"Battle of Cătlăbuga\",\"Battle of Demotika\",\"Battle of Derna (1805)\",\"Battle of Dervenakia\",\"Battle of Dimbos\",\"Battle of Diu (1509)\",\"Battle of Djerba\",\"Battle of Doliana\",\"Battle of Domokos\",\"Battle of Drăgășani\",\"Battle of Dubica\",\"Battle of Dubravnica\",\"Battle of Egri Palanka\",\"Battle of Eperjes\",\"Battle of Eupatoria\",\"Battle of Fidonisi\",\"Battle of Focchies\",\"Battle of Focșani\",\"Battle of Formentera\",\"Battle of Gallipoli (1416)\",\"Battle of Gerontas\",\"Battle of Girolata\",\"Battle of Giurgiu (1595)\",\"Battle of Gorjani\",\"Battle of Gravia Inn\",\"Battle of Grocka\",\"Battle of Heliopolis (1800)\",\"Battle of Hims (1832)\",\"Battle of Hodów\",\"Battle of Ihtiman\",\"Battle of Imbros (1717)\",\"Battle of Jajce (1518)\",\"Battle of Jeddah (1813)\",\"Battle of Kaffa (1616)\",\"Battle of Kagul\",\"Battle of Kamatero\",\"Battle of Karagak\",\"Battle of Karanovasa\",\"Battle of Karpenisi\",\"Battle of Kars\",\"Battle of Kars (1745)\",\"Battle of Karánsebes\",\"Battle of Kassa\",\"Battle of Kerch Strait (1774)\",\"Battle of Kerch Strait (1790)\",\"Battle of Keresztes\",\"Battle of Khotyn (1621)\",\"Battle of Khotyn (1673)\",\"Battle of Khresili\",\"Battle of Kinburn (1787)\",\"Battle of Kirkuk (1733)\",\"Battle of Komarno\",\"Battle of Konya\",\"Battle of Kosovo\",\"Battle of Kosovo (1448)\",\"Battle of Kozludzha\",\"Battle of Koçhisar\",\"Battle of Krasnobród (1672)\",\"Battle of Krbava Field\",\"Battle of Krusevac\",\"Battle of Kulevicha\",\"Battle of Kunovica\",\"Battle of Kurekdere\",\"Battle of Köbölkút\",\"Battle of Kırkdilim\",\"Battle of Kızıl 